    "rich_text_GbXVUF": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_XhCLHT": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "RAM 2500 GVM Upgrades: Carry More, Tow Better, Travel Farther",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "enable_highlight_text_color": true,
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_color": "#56bdc2"
          }
        },
        "text_CfcJd4": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>If you’re ready to get the most from your Ram 2500, getting a GVM upgrade is for you. It isn’t just an upgrade or numbers on paper, Ram 2500 GVM upgrades give you  about changing a number on paper, more support, more rugged potential, and even greater abilities to haul heavy loads of gear. Generally, when you drive your Ram 2500 off the lot, you’ll be sitting in the NB1 category, which is a broad ranging limit when it comes to how much weight you can legally carry. Certain vehicles - like the Ram 2500 - are built for more and can easily be transformed into beasts with upgraded suspension and coils to do your hard-working truck justice. </p><p>If you’re left wanting more - whether that’s more gear, heavier tools, or some serious touring equipment when you’re heading off into the wilds of Australia, our <a href=\"https://www.offroadindustries.com.au/pages/ori-gvm-upgrades\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">GVM upgrades</span></a> can get you there. Discover the freedom of going further and explore the range of RAM 2500 GVM upgrades here at Offroad Industries. <br/><br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_XhCLHT",
        "text_CfcJd4"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.rich-text.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "container": "container",
        "color_schema": "",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "padding_top": 40,
        "padding_bottom": 0,
        "show_section_divider": false,
        "divider_width": "container",
        "custom_id": "",
        "custom_class": "",
        "animations": "inherit"
      }
    },
    "rich_text_jLn8zi": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_XKgGWK": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "GVM Upgrade RAM 2500: Common Questions and What to Ask Your Installer",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "enable_highlight_text_color": true,
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_color": "#56bdc2"
          }
        },
        "text_NxtAw3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Before you commit to a Ram 2500 GVM upgrade pack, there are a few key things worth clarifying regarding your vehicle. First, you’ll want to check how the upgrade changes your total payload and towing limits on your specific truck, along with the Class it’ll be in if you get a certain upgrade completed. </p><p>You’ll also want to check whether your current <a href=\"https://www.offroadindustries.com.au/collections/4-play-wheels\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">wheels</span></a> and tyres are up for the job. With greater weight acting on them, along with a change in ground clearance, you may need to upgrade those too. </p><p>Finally, you might have questions regarding the timeframe and paperwork sign off, which we can help you with. If you have questions and want to speak to our team, <a href=\"https://www.offroadindustries.com.au/pages/contact-us\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">contact us</span></a> any time for more information. <br/><br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_XKgGWK",
        "text_NxtAw3"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.rich-text.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "container": "container",
        "color_schema": "",
